 4630 Q 1651 4813 2131 4813 L 2131 4813 z\nM 2138 4365 Q 1850 4365 1613 4249 Q 1376 4134 1238 3939 Q 1101 3744 1101 3488 Q 1101 2906 1760 2758 L 2419 2605 Q 2509 2579 2633 2649 Q 2758 2720 2880 2854 Q 3002 2989 3078 3161 Q 3155 3334 3155 3514 Q 3155 3891 2880 4128 Q 2605 4365 2138 4365 L 2138 4365 z\nM 2144 384 Q 2675 384 2988 614 Q 3302 845 3302 1235 Q 3302 1530 3142 1715 Q 2982 1901 2624 1984 L 1792 2189 Q 1696 2214 1555 2153 Q 1414 2093 1273 1961 Q 1133 1830 1033 1648 Q 934 1466 934 1248 Q 934 838 1244 611 Q 1555 384 2144 384 L 2144 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p6a92af49b8\"><rect x=\"47.558\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 2 · Payback (months)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Porto</b> pays back in about 7 months: weaker competition means a large share, hosts are cheap to recruit, and guest marketing is low.</p> <p>Lisbon has the most demand, but Hearthstay would win only 12%, hosts cost $600 each to win from rivals, and 8% of each booking goes on marketing, leaving 7% of the booking as contribution. Payback: about 14 months.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> in marketplaces, the best city is where you can become the leader, not the biggest market.</p>"},{"q":"What would you check before committing to Porto?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Seasonality:</b> is demand spread through the year, or concentrated in summer?</li><li><b>Regulation:</b> local short-let licence rules and caps</li> <li><b>Network effect:</b> guests from Spain may book Porto, so cross-promotion could lower guest marketing further</li><li>Whether Lisbon could follow once Porto proves the model</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Launch in Porto first. It pays back in about 7 months, against about 14 for Lisbon, because weak competition lets Hearthstay win a large share with cheap hosts and little guest marketing. Lisbon is the biggest market, but strong rivals would keep Hearthstay's share small and its costs high. Risks: seasonality and short-let licensing in Porto. Next step: recruit 50 hosts as a pilot before full launch, then reconsider Lisbon once the region is established.","great":["Builds supply needs from demand (hosts per night booked)","Compares payback, not market size","Explains why share matters more than size in marketplaces","Checks seasonality and regulation"],"id":74,"slug":"hearthstay"}